          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A researcher investigated two species of mites: a predator and its prey. At the start of a week,\nthere was an equal number of the two species. At the end of the week, the number of prey had\nincreased by $1400\\%$ of the number of prey at the start of the week, and the number of predators\nhad increased by $170\\%$ of the number of predators at the start of the week. The number of\npredators at the end of the week was $p\\%$ less than the number of prey at the end of the week.\nWhat is the value of $p$ ?"
        }
